<title>GERMANY: ADtranz to make profit in 96, rise in 97.</title>
<headline>ADtranz to make profit in 96, rise in 97.</headline>
<dateline>KASSEL 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>ADtranz chairman Kaare Vagner said on Tuesday he expected the rail technology company to make a profit in 1996 and that the profit would rise in 1997.</p>
<p>&quot;We will report a black figure in 1996 and a higher profit in 1997,&quot; Vagner said in an interview with Reuters.</p>
<p>The chairman also said he expected the company's 1996 sales to total around seven billion marks.</p>
<p>ADtranz was formed late last year by German industrial group Daimler Benz and the Swiss/Swedish company Asea Brown Boveri.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
